+  // ---- solution_path_check CLEARANCE_PREDICATE_ADAPTIVE ---------------------
+  // Planner waypoints are discrete states, not path edges: a waypoint is
+  // skipped only when, for every constraint of the last waypoint that passed
+  // the exact predicate (the anchor), margin - sum_v c_v*|q_v - anchor_v| >= 1 µm
+  // (the ADAPTIVE lemma bounds every body's displacement between any two
+  // configurations by its lever bound, so every pair keeps its limit and
+  // every site-workspace box stays inside), joint bounds hold, the deadline
+  // has not passed and, for segments with contact permission or supports,
+  // the state-dependent single-carton rules pass exactly at that waypoint.
+  // Every other waypoint takes the unchanged exact predicate (the caller's
+  // isStateFeasible); a failing waypoint never becomes an anchor. Single
+  // carton search and output phases use the same pair limits (the search
+  // payload reserve exists only for the transit stage), so the proof is that
+  // of the sent-path audit. The set of invalid waypoints is unchanged.
+  bool adaptiveSolutionCheck() const {return adaptive_solution_;}
